turns.text:
I can’t determine this from the available Human Protein Atlas tools.

The tools provide individual-gene blood-expression lookups and tissue-expression classifications, but they do not expose a dataset containing, for every protein:

- blood concentrations measured by both immunoassay and mass spectrometry;
- the numerical immunoassay and mass-spectrometry concentrations;
- the tissue-enriched classification needed to partition the full paired dataset.

Consequently, I cannot calculate the two group sizes, medians, median difference, protein-level ratios, or produce the requested scatter and bar charts without estimating or inventing values. A downloadable HPA blood-concentration table containing both assay types, together with the liver-enrichment labels, would be required.

